  "tuyaKeyHelpTitle": "Finding the local key",
  "tuyaKeyHelpBody": "Each device has a secret local key, given to it when it is set up in the Smart Life app. ZT Home needs it once, to talk to the device directly.\n\nThe easy way: go back and use \"Link Smart Life\", which reads the keys of all your devices.\n\nBy hand, on Tuya's developer site:\n\n1. Sign up for free at iot.tuya.com and create a cloud project.\n2. In the project, open Devices, choose Link App Account and scan the code with the Smart Life app.\n3. In API Explorer, run \"Query Device Details\" with the Device ID below, and copy \"local_key\" from the answer.\n\nThe key is saved encrypted in your ZT account. It never leaves your devices unencrypted.",
